# ring-timeline's SEED Ring refresh token. Copy to ring-timeline.env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# This MUST be its own Ring session — NEVER paste ring-mqtt's token here. Ring rotates refresh
# tokens on use, so two processes sharing one token invalidate each other and the live camera
# integration drops offline. Same Ring account is fine; a separate login is the point.
#
# Mint one in a real terminal (it prompts for email, password, then a 2FA code):
#     npx -y -p ring-client-api ring-auth-cli
#
# The token is ~1.2 KB on ONE line — terminals wrap it and a short copy is silently truncated
# (it will base64-decode to invalid JSON and every request 502s). Verify the whole thing landed.
#
# Only a seed: after first boot ring-timeline writes each rotation to /data/refresh-token on the
# ring-timeline-data PVC, and this value goes stale. Losing that PVC means minting a new token.
RING_REFRESH_TOKEN=replace-with-a-dedicated-ring-refresh-token
